# Firewall rollback safety net — managed by Ansible (roles/firewall).
#
# What: Disables ufw entirely.
# Why:  If a host-firewall apply gets the SSH allow rule wrong, this is the
#       only remote recovery path — beelink alone is a 1.5h drive away (see
#       docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-19-host-firewalls-design.md "Lockout
#       safety"). Triggered only by firewall-rollback.timer, which the role
#       arms before touching any rule and disarms only after Ansible proves it
#       can reconnect through the new rules.
# Resolves: a bad firewall apply locking out SSH with no remote recovery path.
[Unit]
Description=Disable ufw if the firewall role's rollback timer was never disarmed

[Service]
Type=oneshot
ExecStart=/usr/sbin/ufw disable
